# Probe (2026-09-30-19-probe.play) found today's actual daily is The Crimson
# Gift again, 25-player normal, HASTENED -- the same instance two earlier
# sessions today already fought (2026-09-30-14: raid-mode direct pull,
# warrior:arms, style=good; 2026-09-30-16: mode=daily, druid:feral,
# style=flee, died alone at 129s to the bond mechanic once HASTENED's early
# enrage made the growing distance lethal). Neither of those was a healer,
# and neither was wander. This is the first druid:restoration under wander in
# any mode (checked the ledger: wander has only ever been sent as guardian,
# paladin:holy/heal roles, shaman:restoration -- never this spec), and the
# first wander-style pull of this fight. wander has no toward- or away-boss
# steering term (direction.md's #1 write-up on this exact style), unlike
# flee's straight-line-away, so the question this asks that -16 could not:
# does a body with *no* deliberate steering at all fare any differently
# against the bond-drift-then-enrage mechanism than one deliberately running.
# class:8 = Druid Heal, confirmed by this session's own probe screenshot
# (third row, third tile) against the daily screen's targets list.
